00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
president biden at the white house this  afternoon defending his decision and  decisions  in the withdrawal of afghanistan let's  bring in former u.s ambassador to the  united nations nikki haley madam  ambassador thanks for joining us  your reaction to the president's speech  this afternoon  it was pretty clear that by the end of  that speech that president biden gave it  was the beginning of the lame duck  presidency for  joe biden i mean he has lost the trust  and confidence of every member of the  military and the military families that  i'm proud to be a part of he's lost the  trust and confidence of our allies who  are now negotiating without us because  they don't know why we're doing what  we're doing he's lost the trust and  confidence of the american people and i  think if you look at the fact that  they're  the jihadists are celebrating in the  streets because  um america was run out of town and by  the way they left them with billions of  dollars worth of equipment and  ammunition as a housewarming present i  mean you couldn't ask for a more  embarrassing humiliating situation than  what we have right now the world is  definitely a more dangerous place just  because we're out of afghanistan does  not mean this war is over  understanding that you would do things  differently and you have a lot of  criticism about where we are at this  point i'd like you to put on your  advisor hat if you are advising this  president let's say your secretary of  state or let's say your vice president  nikki haley  what do you tell this president now  today going forward not looking  backwards about what what to do with the  current situation  i would say stop talking about president  trump  start owning up to what has happened and  the first thing you should do is  immediately start connecting with our  allies  whether it's taiwan whether it's ukraine  whether it's israel whether it's india  australia japan all of them and reassure  them that we will have their back and  that we need them as well secondly we  need to make sure that we are going on  an anti-terrorist effort across the  world because we are now going to see  with this  moral victory that the jihadists have  you're going to see a heavy recruitment  campaign around the world you're going  to see more lone wolf situations we need  to make sure we're protected we need to  make sure our cyber security is strong  because  actors like russia are going to continue  to hack us because we show no signs of  willing to fight back we need to watch  china because i think you're going to  see china make a move for bagram air  force base and i think they're also  making a move in afghanistan and trying  to use pakistan to get stronger to go  against india so we've got a lot of  issues the biggest thing he should do is  strengthen our allies strengthen those  relationships modernize our military and  make sure we're prepared for the cyber  crimes and the terrorist crimes that are  headed our way yeah it's a big job  handling all of that but another thing  that has just popped up again is north  korea and the restarting of the nuclear  reactor at yongbyon you dealt with north  korea as the ambassador to the united  nations uh president trump obviously had  a very different  perspective when it came to that  your thoughts on this development  you know we led the charge on three  different sanctions packages against  north korea that totally neutralized  them what you're seeing kim do now is  basically he senses the weakness of  biden and so he's going to go ahead and  start getting aggressive his hope is  that he's going to get the united  nations to shake he's going to get other  countries around the world to shake to  lift sanctions to start sending them  money it's the last thing we should do  we should not do that the next thing  biden needs to do is to stand firm on  those sanctions he needs to make sure he  doesn't acknowledge the taliban as a  credible government he needs to also  make sure that he's strong and stays out  of the iran deal these are all going to  be very important issues that he has to  face going forward and he can't show any  weakness whatsoever you know we just had  this ceremony the trend the  bringing the bodies back  at dover  air force base in delaware and the  president and the first lady went as  well as the secretary of defense  and met with the families there as those  bodies were coming in the ultimate pain  would be to lose a son or daughter and  have to bury  your son or daughter and you can feel  that pain when they talk about it but i  was surprised by  how they characterized president biden  who's known for his empathy at least in  the past  of dealing with this moment let's take a  listen  we didn't want to deal with him we  didn't want to we didn't want him  anywhere near us it didn't go well  he talked a bit more about his own son  than we did my son and that that didn't  sit well with me he would not look us in  the eye there was not a  ounce of sympathy looking at his face it  was his his son and about him and  nothing to do with the 13.  first of all are you surprised about  that and second of all you've dealt with  families who've lost in 2015 and the  mother emanuel church when you're  governor of south carolina  what did you do there  i mean it's heartbreaking and i'll tell  you it's even closer to home than that  i'm the wife of a combat veteran who  deployed to afghanistan um we held our  breath the entire time they were gone  because we were scared that that that we  were going to have a knock on our door  and i hurt for those 13 families that  got a knock on their door and i heard  even more that they met with a president  that was completely tone deaf you don't  talk about the death of your own son  when you're talking about loss of life  of a military service man or woman this  is something that is the whole military  family feels this we're bonded by this  we're heartbroken by this and the one  thing you do is you sympathize with them  you hold them you hug them you let them  know that the greatness of their family  member and how the country is better for  them but i get why he didn't look them  in the face how could he look them in  the face when he knew he was the reason  that they died how could he look them in  the face when he knew that they didn't  close that gate and protect those  soldiers how does he look those families  in the face when those poor service men  and women who were doing their job had  to rely on the taliban a jihadist group  for protection that's why he couldn't  look him in the face that's why all he  could do was talk about beau was because  this is wrong on every level and we need  to wrap our arms around those military  families they didn't deserve this and  those men and women are heroes and  they'll be heroes for life  former ambassador to the united nations  nikki haley madam ambassador we  appreciate your time hey sean hannity  here hey click here to subscribe to fox  news youtube page and catch our hottest  interviews and most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else

